# Contributing to CymbalShop E2E Test Suite

Thank you for your interest in contributing to this project. We welcome bug reports, test improvements, documentation updates, and feature enhancements.

## How to Contribute

You can contribute in several ways:

- Report bugs or issues
- Improve or add end-to-end test coverage
- Fix failing tests
- Improve documentation
- Suggest or implement product improvements

## Getting Started

1. Fork the repository and clone your fork locally.
2. Create a branch for your work:
   ```bash
   git checkout -b feature/your-change-name
3. Set up the project dependencies by following the instructions in the README.
4 .Make your changes and validate them locally before opening a pull request.

## Development Workflow
Before submitting a change:

-Keep your changes focused and scoped to one issue or feature.
-Write or update tests for behavioral changes.
-Follow the existing code style and naming conventions.
-Remove debug code and keep the changes clean.
-Update documentation when behavior changes.

## Running Tests
Use the project’s standard validation commands before submitting your PR. For example:

```bash
npm install
npm test
If the repo uses Playwright or another E2E framework, run the relevant test command as documented in the README, for example:

```bash
npx playwright test

## Pull Request Guidelines
When opening a pull request:

-Include a clear title and description of the change
-Reference the issue being addressed, if applicable
-Explain the reason for the change and any trade-offs
-Include screenshots or test output when relevant
-Ensure all relevant checks pass before requesting review

## Code Review
Contributions will be reviewed for:

-correctness
-test coverage
-readability
-maintainability
-alignment with the project goals
We appreciate your time and effort in improving the project.

## Questions?
If you have questions, feel free to open an issue or reach out through the project communication channels.
